   2. Permitted Uses.

   Developer may:

   (a) Integrate the SDK into Developer's application to implement in-app
       purchase functionality;
   (b) Use the SDK for development and testing purposes;
   (c) Distribute and redistribute applications developed with the SDK;
   (d) Conduct reasonable security research to test SDK security;
   (e) Use the SDK for internal business purposes.

   3. Restrictions.

   Developer may not:

   (a) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to derive
       source code from the SDK;
   (b) Modify, alter, or create derivative works of the SDK;
   (c) Redistribute or provide the SDK to third parties without
       authorization;
   (d) Use the SDK to interfere with or conduct denial-of-service attacks
       on OneStore services;
   (e) Develop or deploy functionality designed to bypass or manipulate
       the payment process;
   (f) Conduct fraudulent, illegal, or infringing transactions;
   (g) Use the SDK in third-party applications without authorization.

   4. Payment Integration.

   The SDK is an API wrapper for the OneStore payment system. Actual
   payment processing is performed on OneStore servers. Developer must
   comply with the following:

   (a) Maintain and do not manipulate the integrity of the payment flow
       provided by the SDK;
   (b) The SDK does not expose credit card data; Developer shall not
       store, log, or process such data;
   (c) Display accurate product prices and payment terms to users;
   (d) Handle payment errors and failures appropriately and notify users;
   (e) Cooperate with OneStore's fraud prevention efforts and report
       suspicious transactions.

   PCI DSS Compliance: The SDK does not expose credit card data to
   Developer, therefore Developer is not required to obtain PCI DSS
   certification.

